#: ../../source/docs/rover-failsafes.rst:5
#: a9209ab096044acfab12586a1f64f159
msgid "Failsafes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-failsafes.rst:7
#: 9ddca4c55f254654bf0b7e405be5253a
msgid "Rover supports three failsafe mechanisms as described below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-failsafes.rst:10
#: 7140f0af2d78488897a2087a6a6d105d
msgid "Radio Failsafe (aka Throttle Failsafe)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-failsafes.rst:15
#: 0ad432f59a644504acafdbeaa6e94581
msgid "This failsafe is triggered if the connection between the user's transmitter and the receiver on the vehicle is lost for at least :ref:`FS_TIMEOUT <FS_TIMEOUT>` seconds (default = 1 sec)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-failsafes.rst:17
#: c9e86c3580074fbfb87b92b93e0103f2
msgid "the loss of transmitter/receiver connection is detected by:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-failsafes.rst:19
#: 7a09433a072b470580c82e9ec5766e97
msgid "no signals being sent from the receiver to the autopilot board OR"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-failsafes.rst:20
#: 62f402b682c64e96a81b9198850034a2
msgid "the throttle channel (normally input channel 3) value falling below the :ref:`FS_THR_VALUE <FS_THR_VALUE>` parameter value OR"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-failsafes.rst:21
#: 23550e33dea1425b9fd0b4530ac9c293
msgid "RC_OVERRIDES are lost if :ref:`using a GCS only <common-gcs-only-operation>` is being used,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-failsafes.rst:23
#: 4515dd6e9e3841eeb44e590f128ba661
msgid "if :ref:`FS_ACTION <FS_ACTION>` is \"1\", the vehicle will :ref:`RTL <rtl-mode>` to home, if \"2\" the vehicle will :ref:`Hold <hold-mode>`, if \"3\" or \"4\" the vehicle will attempt to use :ref:`SmartRTL <smartrtl-mode>` but if this mode cannot be engaged the vehicle will :ref:`RTL <rtl-mode>` or :ref:`Hold <hold-mode>` respectively. If \"5\", it will Disarm. \"6\" will switch to :ref:`Loiter mode <loiter-mode>` if possible, else to :ref:`Hold mode <hold-mode>`. switch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-failsafes.rst:24
#: 397249fc164e4cdf8d5c0cc1a01419c8
msgid "once the transmitter/receiver connection is restored, the user must use the transmitter's mode switch to re-take control of the vehicle in :ref:`Manual <manual-mode>` (or any other mode)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-failsafes.rst:27
#: acbc72c2082442b5b9dc58ee85090a89
msgid "Battery Failsafe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-failsafes.rst:31
#: 38550b3b1ca94185b5ed67219ec4e4f8
msgid "This failsafe requires the vehicle have a working :ref:`Power Module <common-powermodule-landingpage>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-failsafes.rst:33
#: 2fc2f2368a6d448ca692cd575cef3b73
msgid "ArduPilot supports up to 10 batteries/power monitors. All the  discussion below applies to those optional batteries also. Each can trigger a failsafe and each can have different actions and setup values. In addition, a group of batteries can be treated as a single unit, see ``BATTx_MONITOR`` = 10."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-failsafes.rst:36
#: 0e2219c302cc4279a5f7fb42067152ab
msgid "When the failsafe will trigger"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-failsafes.rst:38
#: 812ba2898dd74f269b84b15acdd17f51
msgid "If enabled and set-up correctly the battery failsafe will trigger if the main battery's"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-failsafes.rst:40
#: b03adf3bdad54b53a22eb23a136f84d7
msgid "voltage drops below the voltage held in the :ref:`BATT_LOW_VOLT <BATT_LOW_VOLT>` parameter (or FS_BATT_VOLTAGE in older versions) for more than 10 seconds. If set to zero (the default value) the voltage based trigger will be disabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-failsafes.rst:41
#: d2c68bb0effd4923b663bd3bb8a8bf9e
msgid "remaining capacity falls below the :ref:`BATT_LOW_MAH <BATT_LOW_MAH>` parameter (or FS_BATT_MAH in older versions) 20% of the battery's full capacity is a good choice (i.e. \"1000\" for a 5000mAh battery).  If set to zero (the default) the capacity based trigger will be disabled (i.e. only voltage will be used)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-failsafes.rst:44
#: ba7ebda547a74884a44d6bf3e0b8e87c
msgid "What will happen"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-failsafes.rst:46
#: 51f3ac2287504ff9b859a386d5e344bc
msgid "When the failsafe is triggered:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-failsafes.rst:48
#: 22cd803988fd4f37a4bfe3b669c9acbe
msgid "Buzzer will play a loud low-battery alarm"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-failsafes.rst:49
#: 1566c865f78b499d887331782025fb25
msgid "LEDs will flash yellow"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-failsafes.rst:50
#: ab418bc1800e4c059993ac320b960b9f
msgid "A warning message will be displayed on the ground station's HUD (if telemetry is connected)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-failsafes.rst:51
#: cc413073bfde4d3b8b3bd2b3081a32d1
msgid ":ref:`BATT_FS_LOW_ACT <BATT_FS_LOW_ACT>` configures the failsafe action to take.  \"0\" to take no action (default), \"1\" to change into :ref:`RTL <rtl-mode>`, \"2\" to change to :ref:`Hold <hold-mode>`, if \"3\" or \"4\" the vehicle will attempt to use :ref:`SmartRTL <smartrtl-mode>` but if this mode cannot be engaged the vehicle will :ref:`RTL <rtl-mode>` or :ref:`Hold <hold-mode>` respectively.  \"5\" will disarm the vehicle. \"6\" will switch to :ref:`Loiter mode <loiter-mode>` if possible, else to :ref:`Hold mode <hold-mode>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-failsafes.rst:54
#: 0d6df2575e674801a7f4f511c61e4d7c
msgid "Two-Stage Battery Failsafe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-failsafes.rst:56
#: f99621422793414f8e12eaa4fd0f16ff
msgid "Rover also includes a two-layer battery failsafe.  This allows setting up a follow-up action if the battery voltage or remaining capacity falls below an even lower threshold."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-failsafes.rst:58
#: 20196f7ca7204644a64e27238adbac4e
msgid ":ref:`BATT_CRT_VOLT <BATT_CRT_VOLT>` - holds the secondary (lower) voltage threshold.  Set to zero to disable. Default is zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-failsafes.rst:59
#: e53419da9d5e41bb9b1bf6b6973e4eb5
msgid ":ref:`BATT_CRT_MAH <BATT_CRT_MAH>` - holds the secondary (lower) capacity threshold.  Set to zero to disable. Default is zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-failsafes.rst:60
#: 4da7442db0f7486d819d128e3cd61c40
msgid ":ref:`BATT_FS_CRT_ACT <BATT_FS_CRT_ACT>` - holds the secondary action to take. It has the same options and default as :ref:`BATT_FS_LOW_ACT <BATT_FS_LOW_ACT>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-failsafes.rst:63
#: 610ff756791940f98e3b3ad4f455c136
msgid "Advanced Battery Failsafe Settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-failsafes.rst:65
#: 35314a9b7c104901aaf3edf56fb8d179
msgid ":ref:`BATT_FS_VOLTSRC <BATT_FS_VOLTSRC>` allows configuring whether the raw battery voltage or a sag corrected voltage is used"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-failsafes.rst:66
#: e0ebfbf7545e4e97858e168f4df1fcac
msgid ":ref:`BATT_LOW_TIMER <BATT_LOW_TIMER>` can configure how long the voltage must be below the threshold for the failsafe to trigger (10 sec default)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-failsafes.rst:67
#: 7dac386ef41d4f6fa2a7ff9339943ce6
msgid "``BATTx_`` parameters can be setup to trigger the failsafe on other batteries"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-failsafes.rst:70
#: 80024bd8d5454ee88669a07fd99df97e
msgid "GCS Failsafe (aka Telemetry Failsafe)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-failsafes.rst:71
#: 120e259236794744a805fa5d97f00818
msgid "The Ground Station Control (GCS) failsafe controls how Rover will behave if contact with the GCS is lost. The GCS failsafe monitors the time since the last MAVLink heartbeat from the GCS. If no heartbeat is received :ref:`FS_GCS_TIMEOUT <FS_GCS_TIMEOUT>` seconds (Default is 5 seconds), the GCS failsafe event will trigger based on your parameter settings. Note that if no GCS is ever connected, the GCS failsafe will remain inactive regardless of parameter settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-failsafes.rst:75
#: d4ae9d616bed4c7399ee5644682cc408
msgid "Enabling the failsafe in all versions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-failsafes.rst:77
#: 93b9f001fd6a45b1afd39c685d48862e
msgid "In parameters list, set the :ref:`FS_GCS_ENABLE <FS_GCS_ENABLE>` parameter to:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-failsafes.rst:79
#: aab2501cf3404bf397bf2bb1b4c02781
msgid "**Disabled** (Value 0) will disable the GCS failsafe entirely."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-failsafes.rst:80
#: 6f14bf0f28374492bc75eb692d3079df
msgid "**Enabled** (Value 1) will execute the FS_ACTION when Failsafe trigger."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-failsafes.rst:81
#: 26c6e15f2ab1487a9cd3c944f44f2fdf
msgid "**Enabled Continue with Mission in Auto Mode** (Value 2) will ignore the failsafe in an Auto Mode mission."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-failsafes.rst:83
#: b5ef038602e54deb84af7e8e11f66224
msgid "The action done on GCS Failsafe is controlled by the :ref:`FS_ACTION <FS_ACTION>` parameter:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-failsafes.rst:85
#: 083c5f2671fb404988ed09885fa76002
msgid "**Nothing** (Value O) will do nothing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-failsafes.rst:86
#: 0d816056181949da8af55fc961548bfd
msgid "**RTL** (Value 1) will active RTL to go home."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-failsafes.rst:87
#: 13047c3e8a5d43748da5a913f9a73704
msgid "**Hold** (Value 2) will active Hold Mode and stay in place."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-failsafes.rst:88
#: 59676409ecc444de80096f6bfb934711
msgid "**SmartRTL or RTL** (Value 3) will active SmartRTL mode to go back home or RTL if SmartRTL doesn't work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-failsafes.rst:89
#: 277d3093740840e29821061903011dc0
msgid "**SmartRTL or Hold** (Value 4)  will active SmartRTL mode to go back home or Hold mode if Smart RTL doesn't work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-failsafes.rst:91
#: 72b1d77e2a724917bc987e85f0c70c4e
msgid "You must use the transmitter's mode switch to re-take control of the vehicle in :ref:`Manual <manual-mode>` (or any other mode), or change modes with the GCS itself, if communication is re-established."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-failsafes.rst:95
#: 7d551c74d19c4acea7a01da4f7a52dce
msgid "Crash Check"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-failsafes.rst:97
#: 45b3852b9be24e609589e47cdcf3c713
msgid "If enabled by setting the :ref:`FS_CRASH_CHECK <FS_CRASH_CHECK>` parameter to \"1\" (for :ref:`Hold <hold-mode>`) or \"2\" (for :ref:`Hold <hold-mode>` and Disarm) this failsafe will switch the vehicle to Hold and then (optionally) disarm the vehicle if all the following are true for at least 2 seconds:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-failsafes.rst:99
#: 1fa19b2dc9414b11bc781096f2719c4d
msgid "the vehicle is in :ref:`Auto <auto-mode>`, :ref:`Guided <guided-mode>`, :ref:`RTL <rtl-mode>` or :ref:`SmartRTL <smartrtl-mode>` mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-failsafes.rst:100
#: b9ffbf57ac3c4ae29e5a1e007d767621
msgid "velocity falls below 0.08m/s (i.e. 8cm/s)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-failsafes.rst:101
#: db2e6d689b14478f9319193bee2ab42f
msgid "the vehicle is turning at less than 4.5 deg/s"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-failsafes.rst:102
#: d8738f9bb07e431fab3ed929ac4d2d2e
msgid "demanded throttle to the motors (from the pilot or autopilot) is at least 5%"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-failsafes.rst:104
#: 660a705e00344a09bd94b978022dea24
msgid "In addition, the :ref:`CRASH_ANGLE <CRASH_ANGLE>` parameter immediately enables the same actions above if the vehicle's roll or pitch angle exceeds that value. \"0\" disables this check."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-failsafes.rst:107
#: 73354a4c5a66430abb731b19d3576fb0
msgid "Hold Mode Failsafes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-failsafes.rst:109
#: 8eefadb71b9e4bfa857250693260df63
msgid "The :ref:`FS_OPTIONS<FS_OPTIONS>` bitmask parameter determines if failsafes will be recognized while in HOLD Mode. If bit 0 is set, then failsafes will be recognized and acted upon. If not, failsafes will be ignored in HOLD mode (default)."
msgstr ""

